                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ebdf519f-dcf2-337a-bb4b-6abe8c55c215",
                        "entry_id": "c7c3429d-4bca-3e99-b01b-2325430f52d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "One who singles (thins out) plants."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e8f80a1b-624b-4d61-aa4f-dfc24b0fa7b1",
                                "sense_id": "ebdf519f-dcf2-337a-bb4b-6abe8c55c215",
                                "text": "Where the young turnip plants are very thin in the rows they may easily and readily be singled by the hoe alone; but, where turnips are very thick in the rows, it is desirable, if not actually necessary, that singlers should be employed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cad21037-6738-49fa-924d-2f13469bf150",
                                "sense_id": "ebdf519f-dcf2-337a-bb4b-6abe8c55c215",
                                "text": "Their backs were to him, and their heads close to the ground, and of course out of sight, so that they looked like a lot of immense bee-skeps, covered with coarse bags,[…]‘Goodness! gracious! father! what sort of creatures are those!’ ‘Singlers, my boy, Singlers,’ was the reply.[…]‘They are the working people, you know,’ says the father, ‘and they’re always grumbling; they want more money, better houses, shorter hours, and all sorts of things that poor people have no right to think of.’ ‘What shocking creatures!’ replied the son,[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0863677b-385e-4b1d-9ee6-7404be45d0a0",
                                "sense_id": "ebdf519f-dcf2-337a-bb4b-6abe8c55c215",
                                "text": "She’s gone singling, they can’t get singlers enew."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5163cdf3-86dc-4cd5-a69d-1c609e13a81d",
                                "sense_id": "ebdf519f-dcf2-337a-bb4b-6abe8c55c215",
                                "text": "The singler could be provided with means for compensating for an irregular braird."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
